  "result": "All 8 tests pass (5 original plus 3 new).\n\nChanges in `ratelimit/limiter.py`:\n\n- **Refactored refill** into a private helper that computes a key's current tokens as of `now` without storing, so `allow` and `remaining` share the same logic.\n- **`remaining(key, now)`** returns the floored token count after refill, without consuming. A fresh key reports its full limit.\n- **`reset(key)`** drops the key's bucket and any per-key limit override, so the next call behaves like a fresh key.\n- **`set_limit(key, limit)`** stores a per-key override used as both bucket capacity and refill rate over the unchanged window. If the key already has a bucket, its unused tokens are kept and clamped to the new limit. Invalid limits below 1 raise `ValueError`.",
